WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.260
. So, OK, up first, this process.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:09.060
Will Republicans be able to confirm a justice
to replace Ruth Bader Ginsburg before the

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.110
election on November 3rd, before the January
20th inauguration?

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.530
Time wise, 45.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.020
Days, which is what we have roughly remaining
between now and the November 3rd election.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.050
That's very fast.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:26.100
Typically, it takes about 70 days from nomination
to confirmation for a Supreme Court justice.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.720
So it would be very tough to do it in the
45 days before the election.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.850
But it could happen.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:36.379
Donald Trump reportedly going to nominate
a replacement for Ruth Bader Ginsburg this

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:37.379
week.

00:00:37.379 --> 00:00:40.949
The bigger question to me is the lame duck
period.

00:00:40.949 --> 00:00:47.289
If it I don't know that they need to necessarily
do it before the election, because I believe

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:54.629
that even if Joe Biden were to win, they will
have the time and potentially the ability,

00:00:54.629 --> 00:01:00.389
potentially the power, potentially the support
to install a replacement for Ruth Bader Ginsburg

00:01:00.389 --> 00:01:06.470
during the interim period, the lame duck period
between November 3rd, 4th and January 20th.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.210
Now, do they have the votes?

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:14.710
You need 51 votes to confirm a Supreme Court
justice or you need 50 votes, plus the tie

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:20.300
breaking vote from the vice president, which
they would have in Mike Pence for sure.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Republicans have a political situation to
contend with because Republicans are defending

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:29.630
25 of the 38 Senate seats that are on the
ballot.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:36.880
Many of their more vulnerable members have
been eager to get back home, get out of D.C.,

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.780
expected to to be around mid-October.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:45.100
I forget the exact date and campaign and that
would shorten the pre-election period.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.370
It's not really 45 days.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:53.150
It's more like 30 or 35 days because 30 really,
maybe even top 25, because they are planning

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.500
to end this session in mid-October.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:01.460
Now, some of those senators might realize
not only that they need to get back and campaign

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:06.460
because their seats are at risk, but that
pushing forward on this before the election

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.509
could actually be bad for their reelection.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:14.219
The balance right now in the Senate is 53
Republicans and 47 Democrats.

00:02:14.219 --> 00:02:19.879
That's 45 Democrats, plus two independents,
Angus King and Bernie Sanders, who caucus

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:20.959
with Democrats.

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:23.370
So what they need.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:30.260
Those of us what we need who oppose Donald
Trump getting to replace RB, RPG is we need

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:33.190
four Republican senators to say no.

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:38.299
Now, very early, there was this suspicion
or there were rumors that Mitt Romney wasn't

00:02:38.299 --> 00:02:40.810
going to do this before the inauguration.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.389
That was almost immediately refuted by campaign
staff.

00:02:44.389 --> 00:02:46.889
Now, maybe Romney wouldn't do it.

00:02:46.889 --> 00:02:47.889
We don't know yet.

00:02:47.889 --> 00:02:52.609
The early claims that were made were were
merely rumors.

00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:59.280
We then heard from Alaska Republican Senator
Lisa Murkowski, who put out a very carefully

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.630
worded statement saying that, quote, I did
not support taking up a nomination eight months

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:10.469
before the 2016 election to fill the vacancy
created by the passing of Justice Scalia.

00:03:10.469 --> 00:03:16.029
We are now even closer to the 2020 election,
less than two months out.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:18.889
And I believe the same standard must apply.

00:03:18.889 --> 00:03:22.139
So certainly Lisa Murkowski is a No.

00:03:22.139 --> 00:03:23.159
Before the election.

00:03:23.159 --> 00:03:24.200
But there is nothing here.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.400
And this is why you have to look at the wording.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:33.290
There's nothing here that says if Trump loses,
she may still go forward with a vote to confirm

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:37.209
during what would be a lame duck period for
Donald Trump.

00:03:37.209 --> 00:03:39.090
That's really the question mark.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:42.219
Otherwise, we really aren't sure we can speculate.

00:03:42.219 --> 00:03:43.430
Susan Collins.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:44.430
OK.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.090
Maybe she wouldn't go for it before the election.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.659
But what about during the lame duck period?

00:03:49.659 --> 00:03:50.909
Potential lame duck period.

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:53.199
Cory Gardner in Colorado.

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:56.629
He might realize this could be very bad for
his reelection.

00:03:56.629 --> 00:03:59.420
But maybe during the lame duck period, we
don't know.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:05.209
Maybe Martha McSally, who's down to Mark Kelly
in Arizona up.

00:04:05.209 --> 00:04:07.069
We just don't know.

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:09.849
Now we have to look at the hypocrisy.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:13.049
And the reason I'm kind of hesitating is they
don't care.

00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:14.049
They don't care.

00:04:14.049 --> 00:04:15.299
But, yes, they are hypocrites.

00:04:15.299 --> 00:04:18.700
Look at some of these quotes from 2016 and
2018.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.660
Senator Ted Cruz in 2016.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.660
It has been 80 years since a Supreme Court
vacancy was nominated and confirmed in an

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.190
election year.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:31.990
There is a long tradition that you don't do
this in an election year.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:32.990
Hypocrite.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.640
Lindsey Graham in 2018.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:41.270
If an opening comes in the last year of President
Trump's term and the primary process has started,

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.670
we'll wait to the next election.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:50.210
Marco Rubio, I don't think we should be moving
on a nominee in the last year of this president's

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:51.210
term.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.170
I would say that if it was a Republican president.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:55.870
Well, we're waiting, Marco.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:58.980
Thom Tillis from North Carolina, Republican.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.130
The campaign is already underway.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:06.100
It is essential to the institution of the
Senate and to the very health of our republic

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:13.070
to not launch our nation into a partizan divisive
confirmation battle during the very same time

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:16.090
the American people are casting their ballot.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:20.760
To elect our next president now, I could go
on and on with more and more of these.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:27.290
But ultimately, trumpets have not punished
Republicans for heinous hypocrisy.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:30.490
And I have no reason to believe that they
will this time.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.830
Maybe some individual races could be affected.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.800
But let's circle back around.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.270
Is there anything positive here?

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:43.120
Because it seems like this is a disaster for
America, giving Trump the opportunity to ruin

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.680
things not just for four years, not merely
for eight years, but for decades.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:53.050
The one thing that is very clear to me is
that this has the possibility to hugely and

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:59.060
energize Democratic voters, including left
leaning centrists, anti Trump moderates, and

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:04.470
even many of the never Biden left wingers
since Friday night at 8:00 p.m. Eastern, which

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:08.270
is when the world learned of the passing of
Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:12.490
Small dollar donations have exploded to Democrats.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:19.940
One hundred million dollars were donated in
the 40 or so hours following the death of

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.580
Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.340
People are reacting.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:25.220
People are donating to Biden.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:27.470
People are donating to Democrats nationally.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:32.500
And I do believe this will increase voter
turnout, including early voting, which we

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.270
are already seeing.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:35.860
What can we control here?

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:36.860
OK.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.140
We can't make Republicans be consistent.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:41.890
We can't make Republicans stop being hypocrites.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:45.200
We can't make Republicans good moral people.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.080
We can't control Trump.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:49.970
But we can vote and we can lobby.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:53.590
And we can donate and we can phone bank and
we can call our senators.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:56.310
Let's focus on what we can do.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.990
Let me know on Twitter.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:01.530
What do you expect to see with this open seat?

00:07:01.530 --> 00:08:17.150
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman.

